<title>GERMANY: SWIMMING-EUROPEAN SHORT-COURSE MEDALS TABLE.</title>
<headline>SWIMMING-EUROPEAN SHORT-COURSE MEDALS TABLE.</headline>
<dateline>ROSTOCK, Germany 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medals table after the</p>
<p>first day of finals in the European sprints and short-course</p>
<p>swimming championships on Friday:</p>
<p>		  Gold    Silver    Bronze</p>
<p> Germany	  5	  6	   2</p>
<p> Sweden	   2	  1	   -</p>
<p> Netherlands    2	  -	   -</p>
<p> Czech Republic 1	  -	   2</p>
<p> Poland	   1	  -	   1</p>
<p> Italy	    1	  -	   -</p>
<p> Norway	   1	  -	   -</p>
<p> Romania	  -	  2	   1</p>
<p> Switzerland    -	  1	   2</p>
<p> Britain	  -	  1	   1</p>
<p> Austria	  -	  1	   -</p>
<p> Croatia	  -	  1	   -</p>
<p> Finland	  -	  -	   1</p>
<p> France	   -	  -	   1</p>
<p> Greece	   -	  -	   1</p>
<p> Slovakia	 -	  -	   1</p>
<p> Slovenia	 -	  -	   1</p>
<p>(Note: Two bronze medals were awarded in the men's 200 metres</p>
<p>butterfly)</p>
</text>
